===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|physical}} Free of dirt or impurities.
## Not [[dirty]], [[filthy]], or [[soiled]].
##: {{ux|en|Are these dishes '''clean'''?<br /> Your room is finally '''clean'''!<br />For a baby, happiness is a full bottle and a '''clean''' diaper.}}
##* {{RQ:Belloc Lowndes Lodger|chapter=II|passage=Then his sallow face brightened, for the hall had been carefully furnished, and was very '''clean'''. There was a neat hat-and-umbrella stand, and the stranger's weary feet fell soft on a good, serviceable dark-red drugget, which matched in colour the flock-paper on the walls.}}
## In an [[unmarked]] condition.
##: {{ux|en|Put a '''clean''' sheet of paper into the printer.}}
## {{lb|en|aerodynamics}} Allowing an [[uninterrupted]] flow over [[surface]]s, without [[protrusion]]s such as racks or landing gear.
## {{lb|en|aviation}} Having the [[undercarriage]] and [[flap]]s in the [[up]] position.
##: {{antonyms|en|dirty}}
## [[empty|Empty]].
##: {{ux|en|The cargo hold is '''clean'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|Mister, I want to see a '''clean''' dinner plate or there'll be no dessert for you.}}
## {{lb|en|of metal}} Having relatively few [[impurity|impurities]].
##: {{ux|en|'''clean''' steel}}
# {{lb|en|behavioural}} Free of immorality or criminality.
## [[pure|Pure]], especially [[morally]] or [[religiously]].
##: {{ux|en|Our kids can watch this movie because it is '''clean'''.}}
##* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|51|10|passage=Create in me a '''clean''' heart, O God.}}
##* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|volume=II|poem=St. Simeon Stylites|page=63|passage=Ah! let me knot be fool'd, sweet saints. I trust / That I am whole, and '''clean''', and meet for Heaven.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1914|location=New Zealand|journal=Parliamentary Debates|volume=168|page=195
|passage=I do not think there is any member in this House who will not agree that that is the '''clean''' thing to do. Any member sitting on the Government benches will admit in private that that is the proper course for members who break faith.}}
## Not having used [[drug]]s or [[alcohol]].
##: {{ux|en|I've been '''clean''' this time for eight months.}}
## {{lb|en|of criminal, driving, etc. records}} Without [[restriction]]s or [[penalties]], or someone having such a record.
##: {{ux|en|Unlike you, I’ve never caused any accidents — my record is still '''clean'''!}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} Not in possession of [[weapon]]s or [[contraband]] such as drugs.
##: {{ux|en|I'm '''clean''', officer. You can go ahead and search me if you want.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} Devoid of [[profanity]].
# {{cap|smooth}}, [[exact]], and [[performed]] well.
#: {{ux|en|I'll need a sharper knife to make '''clean''' cuts.}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''clean''' leap over a fence}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Total; utter. {{qual|still in "[[clean sweep]]"}}
#* {{RQ:Howell Epistolae|a. 1655|To the Right Honourable the Earl of Clare|passage=Moreover, I find there are some Words now in ''French'' which are turned to a Countersense {{...}} ''Cocu'' is taken for one whose Wife is light, and hath made him a passive ''Cuckold''; whereas '''clean''' contrary, ''Cocu'', which is the Cuckow, doth use to lay her Eggs in another Bird's Nest.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{cap|cool}} or [[neat]].
#: {{ux|en|Wow, dude, those are some '''clean''' shoes ya got there!}}
# {{lb|en|health|of a person}} {{cap|free}} of [[infection]] or [[disease]].
#* {{quote-web|en|author=HarryBlank|work=w:SCP Foundation|title=Face Time|date=14 October 2023|url=https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/36-face-time|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240523092945/https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/36-face-time|archivedate=23 May 2024|accessdate=23 May 2024|text="Serious as cognitohazard." Lillihammer danced down the corridor towards them, doing little pirouettes and leaping from toe to toe. "Reuben Wirth no longer exists. Gonna have to get Forsythe to do that brain scan to make sure I'm '''clean''', but otherwise yeah. Poof."}}
